      "created_at": "2026-09-05T04:43:24Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-05T04:43:24Z",
      "body": "from claude:\n\nFresh occurrence today, on `fumola-livelit-mvp` at `2e6e2feea8` (a diff that touches no evaluator code), in a local full run \u2014 `Evaluator.Properties` case 005:\n\n```\nFAIL Small step reduction and big step reduction are equal\n\n   Expected: `let y:: y = () in y'\n   Received: `let y:: y' = () in y'''\n\non `let y:: y = () in y (after 3 shrink steps)`\n```\n\nSame mechanism as the reported case, but in a `let` rather than a `fun`, so the freshening divergence is not specific to lambda patterns. This one shrinks to five tokens: `let y:: y = () in y`.\n\nSeed not captured \u2014 the run was piped through `tail`, so the `qcheck random seed:` line was lost. Noting that here so the next person pipes it to a file instead.",
